course: dictionary
lesson: 3758
title: Many meanings of fly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Fly can mean moving through the air, a small insect, a flag waving, or time passing quickly. The words around it show you which meaning to choose.
explain: «In Kai's game a player kept flying through walls, which no honest player can do.» Flying usually means moving through the air, but walls and honest players are clues. A real player cannot fly through walls, so this means the player was cheating.
explain: «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» Here fly means travelling by plane. Check it: put «travelling» into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. It does, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Some meanings come from phrases. «Time flies» means time passes very quickly, and «fly a kite» means make a kite move in the air. Never take the bird meaning when a phrase is in front of you.
fact: Fly can be a verb (fly, flies, flew, flown, flying) or a noun (a fly, flies).
fact: «A fly» means a small insect with two wings, like a housefly.
fact: Flies have 6 legs, and birds, bats and insects are animals that can fly.
fact: «Time flies» means time passes very quickly, and «fly a kite» means make a kite move in the air.
fact: «Wouldn't hurt a fly» means someone is very gentle and kind.
exercise: «The fly buzzed against the window.» What is a fly here? | A zip on trousers | A trip by plane | *A small insect with two wings | A flag on a pole
exercise: «Time flies when we are having fun.» What does this mean? | Time moves backwards | *Time passes very quickly | Clocks stop working | We must hurry to catch a plane
exercise: «In Kai's game a player kept flying through walls, which no honest player can do.» What does this tell you about the player? | They were playing fairly | They built a wall | They were a bird | *They were cheating
test: «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» What does flying mean here? | Waving a flag high on a pole | Climbing a steep hill | Running very fast | *Travelling by plane
test: «A flag flies when it is up on a pole.» What does flies mean? | Gets wet in the rain | Is folded away in a box | *Is up high on a pole | Falls to the ground
exam: Which phrase means something passes very quickly? | Fly away with the birds | *Time flies | Wouldn't hurt a fly | Fly a kite
